    GDPR 306: export a Person's personal data (#325)

    * GDPR 306: export a Person's personal data

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M7WN526GZ20958Q1GMPZ72TT

    * GDPR 306: keep a removed Person findable in the export

    Sign-in ignores person_index.removed_at instead of deleting the row, so a removed non-creator still receives that Organization in the access file. The file now matches session expiry, Edit keys, legacy email tokens, and the zero-retention request.

    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M7WPSKWWENKPF336JPB727PB

    * GDPR 306: name OpenRouter for the CSAM retention limit

    The access file said the model hosts might keep flagged content. OpenRouter is the party that may retain child sexual abuse material, including traffic sent with zdr: true.

    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M7WQHCAXEBNCAERTYW5FWJAK

    ---------

    Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

